---
title: "Free Tool to Redact a PDF Online Privately"
description: "Black out names, emails, phone and account numbers in a PDF. The text under each bar is removed, not covered. Runs in your browser. No upload."
faq:
  - q: "Is the PDF Redactor free?"
    a: "Yes. The tool is free, with no account, no sign-up, no watermark and no limit on how often you use it."
  - q: "Is my PDF uploaded to a server?"
    a: "No. The page has no server code. Your PDF is read, redacted and saved in your browser, and it never leaves your device. The only downloads are the page's code and the optional AI model, which contain no user data."
  - q: "Can someone remove the black bars and read the text under them?"
    a: "No. The tool does not draw bars on top of the old text. It makes each page of the new PDF from an image of the page with the bars already in it. The original text, hidden layers and earlier versions are not in the new file, so there is nothing under the bars to recover."
  - q: "Can I undo a redaction?"
    a: "Before you download, yes. Click a bar to show the text under it again, or click a bar you drew to remove it. After you download, the redacted PDF cannot be undone. Keep your original file if you need it."
  - q: "Is automatic redaction 100% accurate?"
    a: "No automatic tool is perfect. It can miss unusual names or black out words that are not personal. Read every page before you share the PDF, click a bar to show the text under it, and drag on a page to add a bar."
  - q: "Can I redact a scanned PDF?"
    a: "Yes, by hand. A scanned PDF has no text that the tool can read, so it does not find personal data automatically. Drag on each page to draw a black bar over the parts you want to hide."
  - q: "Can I still select or search the text in the redacted PDF?"
    a: "No. Each page of the new PDF is an image, so its text cannot be selected, copied or searched. Links, bookmarks and form fields are also not kept."
  - q: "Can I open a PDF that has a password?"
    a: "No. Remove the password in your PDF app first, then open the PDF in the tool."
